  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet, because the premise doesn't hold. `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel`.\n\n- **Required field:** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` parses `OrderPlaced` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. Its README (lines 27 and 31) lists `channel` as part of the contract and says a missing `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event.\n- **Reporting data:** `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes `channel` into the `orders` table, and `analytics-ingest/src/core/rows.ts:8` defines it as a column.\n- **Effect of removal:** if orders-service stops sending it, every `OrderPlaced` event would fail ingestion with a contract violation.\n- **Not affected:** billing-service doesn't depend on it. Its test already passes `channel: undefined`.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n\n1. **Remove it from the order model and the API input, but keep it on the event.** This only works if `channel` still has a value, so it isn't really a removal.\n2. **Remove it everywhere in orders-service.** This needs analytics-ingest to make `channel` optional or drop it first. That's the other team's repo, which is read-only here, so it would need to be coordinated and released before this change.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now anyway.** I can do this if you've already agreed it with the analytics team. I'd update `order.ts`, `events.ts`, `requestParsing.ts`, the README and the tests.\n\nWhich one do you want?",
